{
  "slug": "obsidian-editor-parity-spec",
  "title": "Obsidian Editor Parity — Technical Spec",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "ingress",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "The implementation spec for "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Obsidian Editor Parity",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": " — the engineering detail behind the goal tree. Storage model "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "A",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": " (skin-on-blocks) and a single shared editor engine are fixed; this doc turns each phase into concrete data-model shapes, render-contract obligations, file touchpoints, and acceptance criteria. Companion to the overview at "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "/papers/obsidian-editor-parity",
          "marks": [
            "code"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "."
        }
      ],
      "id": "b1"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Scope and non-goals",
      "id": "b2"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "In scope: the editing surface and the linked-knowledge layer — Live-Preview canvas, "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "[[wikilinks]]",
          "marks": [
            "code"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": ", "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "![[embeds]]",
          "marks": [
            "code"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": ", "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "^block-refs",
          "marks": [
            "code"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": ", inline "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "#tags",
          "marks": [
            "code"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": ", a backlinks panel, a properties panel, command palette, and a read-only Markdown projection."
        }
      ],
      "id": "b3"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "NOT converging storage to Markdown",
            "marks": [
              "strong"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": " — PortableDoc stays the system of record. "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Source mode",
            "marks": [
              "code"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": " renders a one-way projection."
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "NOT dropping the rich vocabulary",
            "marks": [
              "strong"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": " — diagrams, sheets, asciicasts, schema-field blocks all survive; Obsidian has no equivalent and we keep them."
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "NOT a second editor",
            "marks": [
              "strong"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": " — exactly one engine (the "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "<bp-paper-editor>",
            "marks": [
              "code"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": " Web Component) serves Studio and web."
          }
        ]
      ],
      "id": "b4"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Load-bearing decisions",
      "id": "b5"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Storage A",
            "marks": [
              "strong"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": ": the Obsidian experience is a layer over the block AST. Wikilinks/tags/embeds become new node kinds in the existing inline/block model, NOT Markdown syntax in a text file."
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Unified engine",
            "marks": [
              "strong"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": ": Studio already runs a framework-neutral "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "<bp-paper-editor>",
            "marks": [
              "code"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": " (TipTap/ProseMirror). The web app embeds the same component instead of its read-only React renderer."
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Three renderers stay in lockstep",
            "marks": [
              "strong"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": ": every new node kind ships in all three render sites in the same change (see the render contract below)."
          }
        ]
      ],
      "id": "b6"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Data model — new node kinds",
      "id": "b7"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Today the inline tree ("
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "api/lib/barkpark/portable_doc/render/inline.ex",
          "marks": [
            "code"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": ") has five kinds: "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "text · strong · em · code · link",
          "marks": [
            "code"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": ". Parity adds three inline leaves and one block. All are additive — existing docs are untouched."
        }
      ],
      "id": "b8"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "json",
      "value": "// Inline leaves (additive to inline.ex)\n{ \"type\":\"wikilink\", \"docId\":\"content-graph\", \"label\":\"Content Graph\" }            // [[Content Graph]]\n{ \"type\":\"blockref\", \"docId\":\"content-graph\", \"blockId\":\"b7\", \"label\":\"…\" }        // [[Content Graph#^b7]]\n{ \"type\":\"tag\",      \"name\":\"editor\" }                                             // #editor\n\n// Block-level transclusion — mirrors the existing {type:\"sheet\", ref, snapshot} precedent\n{ \"id\":\"b9\", \"type\":\"embed\",\n  \"ref\":      { \"docId\":\"document\", \"section\":\"Shape of a Document\" },             // ![[Document#Shape…]]\n  \"snapshot\": { \"html\":\"<…cached rendered fragment…>\", \"rev\":4 } }                 // write-through refreshed",
      "id": "b9"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Key design choice: "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "references store the resolved "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "docId",
          "marks": [
            "code"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": " (the stable slug), not the typed title"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": " — the label is display-only and re-resolved on render via "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Content.reference_title/4",
          "marks": [
            "code"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": " ("
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "render.ex",
          "marks": [
            "code"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "). This matches how "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "field-reference",
          "marks": [
            "code"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": " already works, so the content-edge graph picks up wikilinks for free once they project as edges."
        }
      ],
      "id": "b10"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "The three-renderer contract",
      "id": "b11"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "One node kind ⇒ three render sites must change together, plus the editor round-trip. This is the single most important discipline in the epic — a node that renders in one surface and breaks in another is the top regression risk."
        }
      ],
      "id": "b12"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "text",
      "value": "api/lib/barkpark/portable_doc/render/{inline,compose}.ex   # HTML — web reader + Studio View pane\ninternal/pdrender/*.go                                      # terminal (Go)\nweb/components/portable-doc.tsx                             # Next.js read renderer\napi/assets/paper-editor/src/convert.js                      # TipTap <-> portable-doc round-trip (editor)",
      "id": "b13"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Add a parity-matrix test",
            "marks": [
              "strong"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": ": one fixture doc containing every new node kind, asserted byte-stable across all three HTML/terminal/web renderers (extend the existing render snapshot tests)."
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "pdrender degrades gracefully",
            "marks": [
              "strong"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": ": wikilink/tag render as styled text; embed renders the cached snapshot or a labeled box (its unknown-block fallback already exists)."
          }
        ]
      ],
      "id": "b14"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Cross-cutting infrastructure",
      "id": "b15"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "text": "Backlinks — data already exists",
      "id": "b16"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "No new storage. The content-edge graph ("
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "api/lib/barkpark/content/graph.ex",
          "marks": [
            "code"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": ") already computes both directions; the panel is pure presentation:"
        }
      ],
      "id": "b17"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "lang": "elixir",
      "value": "Content.Graph.list_inbound_edges(doc_id, dataset: ds)    # linked mentions (who points here)\nContent.Graph.reverse_referencers(doc_id, [ds, scope])   # same, ranked by topology (distance, in-degree)\nContent.Graph.list_outbound_edges(doc_id, dataset: ds)   # this doc's own links\n# unlinked mentions = full-text scan for title/alias, minus the docs already in inbound_edges",
      "id": "b18"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "text": "Persistence — the op pipeline is unchanged",
      "id": "b19"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "New nodes flow through the SAME patch pipeline: editor emits a "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "patch-block",
          "marks": [
            "code"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": " op → "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "paper-op",
          "marks": [
            "code"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": " LiveView event ("
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "studio_live.ex",
          "marks": [
            "code"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": ") → "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Content.apply_paper_block_op/3",
          "marks": [
            "code"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": " → "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Patch.apply_patch/2",
          "marks": [
            "code"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": " → "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Projection.project/3",
          "marks": [
            "code"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": " re-derives "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "content[body]",
          "marks": [
            "code"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": " and field index. Wikilinks/embeds project into "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "content_edges",
          "marks": [
            "code"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": " via the existing "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "extract_edges/2",
          "marks": [
            "code"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": " pass once they’re recognized as references."
        }
      ],
      "id": "b20"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Phase 1 — Foundation: shared engine + inline infra",
      "id": "b21"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Extract the editor as a reusable core and stand up the inline-node plumbing every later phase builds on. No user-visible Obsidian features yet — this de-risks the unified-engine bet and makes phases 2–5 additive."
        }
      ],
      "id": "b22"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "text": "Files",
      "id": "b23"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "api/assets/paper-editor/src/index.js",
            "marks": [
              "code"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": " — factor the TipTap init + emit pipeline behind a clean embed contract (mount target, doc in/out, op-emit callback)"
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "web/components/portable-doc.tsx",
            "marks": [
              "code"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": " — host "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "<bp-paper-editor>",
            "marks": [
              "code"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": " in read mode; keep SSR fallback"
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "api/lib/barkpark/portable_doc/render/inline.ex",
            "marks": [
              "code"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": " — register wikilink/blockref/tag leaves (render = styled text for now)"
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "api/assets/paper-editor/src/convert.js",
            "marks": [
              "code"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": " — round-trip the new leaves TipTap⇄portable-doc"
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "internal/pdrender/",
            "marks": [
              "code"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": " + "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "web/components/portable-doc.tsx",
            "marks": [
              "code"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": " — text-level render of the new leaves"
          }
        ]
      ],
      "id": "b24"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "text": "Acceptance criteria",
      "id": "b25"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "The same compiled "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "<bp-paper-editor>",
            "marks": [
              "code"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": " bundle mounts and renders a doc in BOTH Studio and the Next.js app"
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "A doc containing wikilink/blockref/tag nodes round-trips editor→save→reload with zero data loss"
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Parity-matrix fixture renders byte-stable across all three renderers"
          }
        ]
      ],
      "id": "b26"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Risk: ",
          "marks": [
            "strong"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "the web app currently has NO editor; embedding a ProseMirror Web Component in Next.js (SSR + hydration) is the unknown. Mitigate by shipping read-mode first."
        }
      ],
      "id": "b27"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Phase 2 — Harvest the substrate (fast wins)",
      "id": "b28"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Three features whose data or block types already exist — highest leverage, lowest risk. Do these first to prove the model before the deep canvas work."
        }
      ],
      "id": "b29"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "text": "Files",
